  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to the sixteenth replenishment of the African Development Fund (AfDF-16)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Development Fund (AfDF) has as its central objective the eradication of poverty in Africa through the promotion of sustainable economic growth and social development. The AfDF seeks to achieve this by providing concessional project and programme loans and grants to governments of low-income countries. The Fund&apos;s financial resources are replenished every three years. The sixteenth replenishment of the AfDF (ADF-16) is taking place during a turbulent period that presents both opportunities and challenges for the poorest countries in Africa. The replenishment negotiations have resulted in a steering document that focuses on achieving &#x201c;A Climate-smart, Resilient, Inclusive and Integrated Africa&#x201d;. AfDF-16 remains committed to the strategic vision of the African Development Bank Group&apos;s Yen Year Strategy and the High 5 operational priorities supporting Agenda 2063 and the 2030 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).</narrative>
  </description>
